{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-13T02:26:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "review_nb_disposition", "ref_id": "CHANGE-0135", "finding": "PR #249 bot sweep (Copilot 5 + Codex 3 threads) after close: two Codex P1s were real functional gaps invisible to CI (runners have no WSL distro) — the success-arm marker path was never wslpath-translated on the WSL branch, and the spawnfail arm's reduced PATH (System32) still exposed wsl.exe, contradicting the spec's own D3 sentence, so a WSL-functional host would route around the decoy.", "decision": "FIXED IN-TREE (e398686): wslpath guard in the sh payload (Git Bash passes through, WSL translates to /mnt); spawnfail PATH now targets the arm's decoy root; sh payloads moved from PS double- to single-quoted literals — this CLOSES the double-quote dollar/backtick interpolation class recorded as FOLLOW-UP in the 2026-08-13T01:26 disposition; text-mode-detail doc drift killed in USER_GUIDE + product doc + engine header; perl dependency in test-aai-doctor.sh replaced with node. All pinned in Pester (139/139).", "residual": "WSL-branch marker translation is proven by payload-shape pin and sh semantics, not by an end-to-end run on a WSL-functional host — no such host exists in CI; first downstream /aai-doctor run on one is the real proof.", "source": "PR #249 review threads (resolved 2026-08-13); commit e398686"}
{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-13T08:02:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "review_nb_disposition", "ref_id": "CHANGE-0136", "finding": "Validation CONDITIONAL-PASS (F-2 LOW SIGPIPE advisory, F-3/F-5 INFO) + review spec PASS / code FAIL (1 BLOCKING, 2 NB) on the CI platform-coverage scope.", "decision": "FIXED IN-TREE (803d4ae): BLOCKING pipe-pin SIGPIPE — review falsified validation's 1-in-1300 LOW estimate with a measured 3-in-11 failure rate and a proven 64KB pipe-buffer cliff (95/100 synthetic); all 42 new-test pipes converted to here-strings, 6/6 consecutive full runs green; NB-1 the WSL-leg doctor exit code is load-bearing via GitHub's appended exit LASTEXITCODE — comment now states the deliberate fail-closed truth. ACCEPTED: NB-2 test_019/020 exit-code and shell pins grep job-wide rather than arm-scoped — bounded by the live-run flip gate which asserts the real per-arm lines; tighten opportunistically. RECORDED: validation F-3 Move-Item negative pins are step-scoped and truthful; F-5 pre-close false-open pair is the standard sequencing state.", "residual": "Spec-AC-01/02/03 remain planned until the named ps1-quality PR run shows the verbatim merge-gate lines (WSL1 CONTROLS OK, WSL ROUTING OK with AAI-BRANCH: WSL, SELFTEST OK 3/124/125, CAT-15 wsl functional, per-leg PESTER OK, 97/98 controls, Resolve-SelfTestEngine to powershell, 5.1-ONLY FALLBACK OK).", "source": "docs/ai/validation/validation-20260813T073331Z-CHANGE-0136-ps1-ci-platform-coverage.md; docs/ai/reviews/review-20260813T074813Z-CHANGE-0136-ps1-ci-platform-coverage.md"}
{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-13T10:50:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "review_nb_disposition", "ref_id": "CHANGE-0137", "finding": "Validation PASS (F-1 LOW: stored RED log lacks a RED_CLASS stamp) + review dual PASS, 0 BLOCKING, 3 NB on the update-doctor-field-report scope.", "decision": "FIXED IN-TREE: NB-1 stdout-flush class — success line now uses process.exitCode with natural drain, and BOTH never-return SKIP paths (emitSkip, config-off) write via fs.writeSync(1) which is synchronous even on the Windows PS async pipe; NB-3 inline_review_scope gains the two omitted changed files (docs/ai/update-config.yaml, docs/INDEX.md). FOLLOW-UP: NB-2 — a UTF-8 BOM hides a FIRST-LINE config key from both column-0 parsers identically (off silently becomes on); fix update-doctor-report.mjs and update-check.mjs TOGETHER, never one side (parity invariant). ACCEPTED: F-1 — the stored RED log keeps its legacy no-RED_CLASS shape (2 of 5 recent logs share it); the validator's independent pre-change-tree replay is the substantive RED proof; stored evidence is never retro-edited. RECORDED: review INFO — ENOBUFS surfaces as the generic spawn-failed reason; Windows timeout kill is not kill-tree (doctor's internal 170s bound is the second net).", "residual": "RR-1..5 unchanged (rollout lag, downstream WSL field report, executed Windows ps1 run, staleness between updates, same-second overwrite).", "source": "docs/ai/validation/validation-20260813T103126Z-CHANGE-0137-update-doctor-field-report.md; docs/ai/reviews/review-20260813T104221Z-CHANGE-0137-update-doctor-field-report.md"}
{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-13T11:22:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "review_nb_disposition", "ref_id": "CHANGE-0137", "finding": "PR #252 bot sweep (Copilot 1 + Codex 4): atomic report publish, timeout tree-kill, BOM-hidden first-line config key, unreadable-config default, swallowed retention failures.", "decision": "FIXED IN-TREE: Codex P1 atomic publish — report now writes to a same-directory .tmp and renames into the canonical name (learned-append.mjs pattern); a crash mid-write can never leave a torn report under the shape-matched name (a rare orphaned .tmp is shape-excluded from both readers and prune). ACCEPTED with layered-bounds rationale: Codex P1 timeout tree-kill — the only long-running doctor child is the CAT-14 selftest which self-bounds at 170s, under the helper's 240s ceiling, so the doctor's own watchdogs fire first; already recorded in the 10:50 disposition. FOLLOW-UP BATCH (config/retention robustness, one ref): Copilot BOM first-line key (== NB-2, fix both parsers together), Codex P2 unreadable-config-defaults-on (D2 safe-direction rationale holds for a read-only diagnostic but a named degrade line would be more honest), Codex P2 silent prune failures (bounded by the one-line output contract; consider a stderr diag).", "residual": "Orphaned .tmp on a crash between write and rename persists until manual cleanup — shape-excluded, milliseconds-wide window.", "source": "PR #252 review threads; commit follows"}
{"v": 1, "ts": "2026-08-13T11:55:00Z", "actor": "orchestrator", "type": "kpi_review", "ref_id": "validation-cost-calibration", "finding": "SPEC-0119 lane-canon KPI checkpoint after the promised ~5 rides (0133-0137): Validation median PRE-0132 = 99970 tokens (56 runs, matches the 99k baseline); POST-0132 median = 136517 (7 runs) - UP 37 percent, not down. Remediation rounds post-0132: 5/3/3/1/1 vs the historical 0-1 typical.", "decision": "KEEP the lane canon, EXTEND the observation window - no rollback. The post-window is maximally confounded: all five rides are the hardest Windows/CI-platform scopes in project history, and their validation depth was deliberately adversarial (scratch-clone RED replays, hang probes, workflow line-by-line reads) with demonstrated catches the shallow lane would have missed (0136 review falsified validation's own SIGPIPE estimate; 0137 hang probe proved the 240s bound exactly). The canon's primary target was DOWNSTREAM blanket full-suite re-runs (27 percent ride cost in the owner's Codex project), which the local flow never did. Next checkpoint: after 5 non-platform rides, like-for-like; AND request one downstream ride timing from the owner after they take the v2026.08.13 release (the real KPI lives there).", "residual": "Local median is a weak proxy for the downstream KPI; remediation-rate uptick tracks scope difficulty (field catches), not lane depth.", "source": "docs/ai/METRICS.jsonl agent_runs re-sum 2026-08-13"}
