{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T14:40:14Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-corpus-header-other-bucket","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"resolveAllCorpus's --all header counts (included plus the five per-status excluded buckets) do not sum to files scanned: a type spec doc whose status is outside the five closed-list statuses, or whose frontmatter fails to parse, is dropped from BOTH the included and excluded lines with no visible signal.","decision":"Flagged as F9 in round-1 validation and carried forward as F13 in round-2; deferred both times without a tracked item. Currently latent on the real corpus (0 parse failures, all statuses covered today), but a future doc landing outside the five statuses would silently understate the disclosed suppressed-count upper bound.","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260814T124933Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round2.md F13"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T15:38:22Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-tdd-skips-full-sweep","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"the TDD role declares done after targeted suites only, so defects visible only to the full framework sweep surface two roles later and cost a whole validate-remediate lap each","decision":"This ride burned roughly 2.5 hours on two extra laps for F0 (spec-lint allowlist) and F10 (CHANGELOG scaffold), both of which only the sweep sees; the cheap suites run early and the 47-minute one runs last, so its findings always arrive after the expensive roles have finished","source":"ticks 104-109, 2026-08-14; sweep is 47 min and nests suites (delta-stage3 to delta-stage2 to spec-lint)"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T15:38:32Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-range-mode-dirty-worktree","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"range mode takes added-line numbers from git diff base...HEAD but reads file content from the worktree, so a dirty tree reports an untouched symbol and misses the changed ones","decision":"Validation round 3 F17, reproduced with a dirty-worktree fixture; bounded to range mode with uncommitted edits and inherited from the frozen spec D3/D4 design rather than an implementation infidelity, so it was not a blocker; wants a dirty-worktree range fixture","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260814T144556Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round3.md"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T16:06:04Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-cliflag-kind-precision","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"extractCliFlags labels every --lowercase-flag token 'cli-flag' regardless of context: on the real tree 30 of 139 cli-flag candidates are CSS custom properties (--accent, --bg, --fg, --muted, --line, --card-bg in generate-docs-hub.mjs / generate-factory-report.mjs) and 35 are flags this repo passes TO external tools (git/gh), not CLI surface of this repo at all -- ~47% of the kind, ~17% of all 390 candidates, carry a factually wrong kind label","decision":"an operator triaging the --all list per the class-4 action ('Remove; file an intake note if genuinely valuable') could delete a CSS custom property believing it is an unrequested CLI flag, silently breaking a page's dark theme; no LIMITS sentence warns that the cli-flag kind includes non-flags. Fix is a design call (rename the kind vs exclude --x: / var(--x) contexts) adjacent to the spec's NO STOPLIST decision, so it is deferred rather than fixed in this remediation pass","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260814T154415Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-2"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-14T22:22:40Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-validation-staleness-undetected","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"a validation pass survives a later remediation that rewrites the validated code, and the default routing skips re-validation","decision":"Round 3 passed at 15:37Z; code review then failed and remediation rewrote the engine, suite, prompt and eight surfaces, yet SPEC-0012 G3 routing sends a pass-with-review-reset straight to rule 13 and never re-fires rule 11. Only the validator noticing its own staleness caught it, and clearing it needed an owner-approved reset-block --force. The verdict should carry the content hash it was taken against so staleness is mechanical, not a matter of an agent volunteering it","source":"observed 2026-08-14, owner decision recorded; state.mjs reset-block refusal message"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T07:03:31Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-subagent-long-wait-never-wakes","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"a subagent waiting on a long background process can miss its own completion and stall indefinitely, holding the whole ride","decision":"Twice in one ride: round 3 armed three backstop waiters that all watched for a Total: line the framework prefixes with colour codes, and round 4 slept five hours after its sweep had already written summary.txt with 79/79. The coordinator read the tally off disk in seconds. Long-running work should be polled from the artifact on disk, never awaited through a pattern-matched waiter","source":"observed 2026-08-14/15, tests/skills/results/test-20260814-223516/summary.txt written 23:07:42Z, agent silent until 03:59Z"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T07:03:31Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-subagent-probe-hits-real-repo","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P1","finding":"a validator probe helper ran git commands against the real repository and created two commits on main","decision":"The helper cd-ed into a fixture inside a command substitution, which runs in a subshell, so the parent shell stayed in the real repo. Repaired with git reset --mixed 5116c36 and verified independently (HEAD restored, main equals origin main, tag intact, nothing pushed), but nothing structurally prevented it: a read-only role mutated the shipping repo and only caught it by luck","source":"validation round 4, 2026-08-14; coordinator verification of HEAD 5116c36 and zero unpushed commits"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T08:14:24.000Z","actor":"ales_holubec.net","type":"hitl_decision","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","decision":"Narrow the class-4 extractor kinds to CONTRACT surfaces only. Drop or default-off mjs-export, sh-func and ps1-func; keep cli-flag (with the CSS-custom-property and external-tool-flag misclassification fixed) and yaml-key.","rationale":"Owner call 2026-08-15: an internal helper is ABSENT from every spec by design, so absence carries no signal for it — the premise only holds for surfaces a requirement is expected to name. Measured: mjs-export 128 + sh-func 64 + ps1-func 53 = 245 of 390 candidates come from kinds that are categorically wrong, matching the review-measured 245 internal helpers; yaml-key was the one kind where suppression discriminated.","authority":"owner","amends":"frozen spec D3 extractor-kind set and its dependent AC rows","acceptance":"every remaining candidate must be defensible in one sentence stating why a requirement should have named it; raw count expected to drop from 390 to tens","origin_error":"intake assumption A2 listed five extractor kinds without asking whether each is a contract surface; Planning inherited it and validation checked fidelity to a spec that was wrong"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T08:47:50Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up_status","id":"fu-deslop-cliflag-kind-precision","status":"done","resolved_by":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","source":"tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh:TEST-015"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T10:48:17Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-adjudication-self-suppression","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"writing the list of indefensible candidates into the spec made the engine suppress them, because any mention in a requirement doc counts as the requirement naming the symbol","decision":"Live count fell from 70 to 58 and suppressed rose from 398 to 410 the moment the adjudication summary landed in the frozen spec; the block says these flags are NOT requirements and the engine reads it as proof that they are. Self-inflicted instance of the prose-suppression false-negative class the LIMITS block already discloses, and it means documenting a finding can erase it","source":"observed 2026-08-15T10:48Z, before/after the adjudication summary was folded into docs/specs/SPEC-DRAFT-spec-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:31:29Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-external-call-shape-gaps","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"The .mjs external-tool exclusion (D3) misses two call shapes: (a) a subprocess call whose command is an expression rather than a string literal, e.g. execFileSync(ghBinOf(opts), [... '--jq' ...]) in hitl-channel.mjs:233 leaks gh's --jq; (b) an argv array built and returned by a helper function rather than a local const, e.g. buildGhArgs() in aai-issues.mjs:235 leaks gh's --state.","decision":"Round-6 validation's independent cross-check (V6-4) found both gaps by reimplementing D2+D3 from scratch and diffing against the engine. Both sites are currently corpus-suppressed (not in the live 58/68 candidate output), so live impact is nil today, and the degrade direction is safe: an unresolvable command word conservatively keeps the flag as a candidate rather than dropping it. Fixing requires engine logic changes, out of scope for this documentation-only remediation pass.","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260815T110436Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round6.md section 4 and Findings V6-4"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:31:29Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-external-bin-words-closed-list","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"EXTERNAL_BIN_WORDS (the .sh/.ps1 external-tool recognizer in D3) is a closed, hardcoded 10-binary list (git, gh, cargo, rg, wrangler, tsc, wsl, sed, npm, npx). A binary outside this list, e.g. grep --color=auto, yields --color as a live candidate instead of being excluded.","decision":"Round-6 validation (V6-5) confirmed via an independent fixture. The list is fully disclosed in D3 and is process-based (context-keyed), not a per-flag stoplist, so it does not violate the NO STOPLIST rule -- but it carries the same rot risk a curated list always does. Extending or generalizing it is an engine-logic change, out of scope for this documentation-only remediation pass.","source":"docs/ai/validation/validation-20260815T110436Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine-round6.md Findings V6-5"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:48:56Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-all-corpus-specs-only","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P2","finding":"The --all requirement corpus is docs/specs/** with type: spec only; a flag or config key requested in docs/issues/** or docs/rfc/** is not suppressed and still reports as an unrequested-surface candidate.","decision":"Measured on the live 68-candidate run: 15 of 54 distinct cli-flag symbols (28%) are named in docs/issues or docs/rfc, including --worktree-guard and --worktree-baseline (requested in CHANGE-0125:56) and --pr-config (requested in CHANGE-0096:38). An operator triaging the --all list per the class-4 action would remove a flag a human explicitly asked for, with nothing in the output pointing them at docs/issues/. D2 already treats an intake as a requirement document for --diff; the same reasoning is not applied to --all. NOTE: widening the corpus to docs/issues/** would re-trigger the self-suppression coupling recorded in the CHANGE intake's Adjudication Summary (NB-3) — the 10-row indefensible table currently sits outside the --all corpus only because docs/issues/** is excluded.","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260815T114500Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-2"}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-08-15T11:48:58Z","actor":"orchestrator","type":"follow_up","id":"fu-deslop-test014-no-restore-trap","ref_id":"deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine","severity":"P3","finding":"tests/skills/test-aai-deslop.sh:916 TEST-014 runs generate-docs-hub.mjs against the real repo and restores docs/SKILL_CATALOG.html and docs/skill-catalog-data.json from mktemp copies at the end of the function, with no trap.","decision":"A timeout kill from the harness's AAI_TEST_TIMEOUT, a Ctrl-C, or a future return added between the generator invocation and the two cp restores would leave the operator's working tree with a modified tracked catalog file and orphaned mktemp files, showing up as unexplained scope pollution in a pre-PR sweep.","source":"docs/ai/reviews/review-20260815T114500Z-deslop-scope-and-unrequested-engine.md NB-7"}
